  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM &#x2013; Multi Country Humanitarian Assistance &#x2013; CAP 2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Northern Mozambique is facing an ongoing complex crisis marked by a dire humanitarian situation. For over four years, northern Mozambique has experienced attacks by non-state armed groups allegedly affiliated with the Islamic State, resulting in large scale displacements. The complex crisis has led to large displacement over the past four years. According to IOM, 946,505 internally displaced persons are currently internally displaced in northern Mozambique (Displacement Tracking Matrix - DTM, June 2022). The dire humanitarian situation in northern Mozambique is therefore not only fueled by the humanitarian needs of the displaced persons, many of whom have been forced to flee multiple times, but also by the needs of the host communities, who have continued to show solidarity in the face of increasingly scarce resources and stretched services. In order to address the acute needs of displaced and vulnerable migrants in Cabo Delgado, IOM is providing comprehensive and integrated emergency health and DTM intervention, with the main objective to ensure dignified, safe and secure living conditions and basic services for vulnerable populations affected disasters driven by natural hazards and conflict.</narrative>
  </description>
